INSTALLATION
------------

see http://www.symfony-project.org/getting-started/1_4/en/

RUN TESTS
---------

In order to run an individual test:
```sh
php test/unit/response/sfResponseTest.php
```

To run all tests, it's recommended to use the task provided by Symfony. This requires a valid Symfony project, so if you don't have one, you can create a temporary project:
```sh
php data/bin/symfony generate:project test-project
```

Now you can run the task:
```sh
php symfony test:all
```

If you don't have PHP 7 installed locally, you can use Docker to run PHP quickly:
```sh
docker run --rm -v "$PWD":/app -w /app php:7.4-cli php <MY PHP COMMAND>
```